  "label": "mocking and contemptuous emotion",
  "description": "The meme expresses a mocking and contemptuous emotion by juxtaposing a smiling Black teenager with a gorilla and using the text 'be careful who you call ugly in high school' to imply that calling someone 'ugly' could lead to them being perceived as a gorilla. This is a dehumanizing and racially derogatory stereotype that mocks and degrades Black individuals. The emotion is conveyed through the visual contrast and the coded racial slur implication in the text.",
